{"title":"2024 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The line with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019ebcb038db887125d81df1b3d65645b84fabe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3x+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> is reflected in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis. What is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercept of the new line?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25a0b24ada568d603142ad6b12b460fdd91643b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ -2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ -6 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"436\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When a line or point is reflected in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is negated (e.g. reflecting the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1c720139325a2c3491ba41476d225311fcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis would result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad54ab653d3aa7be3416107a9e3ea47007d12f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p><p>This means that the new line would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7100cf8b3bd7ba728cf8ef4db40b58a96821e274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -3x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>With this new line, we can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> to find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercept:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/5693b9f97ae969ff42883a22f9cbc7a0de32a3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = -3x_0 + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7447a7ca525a72c7a09c1d2e7341ef98341b6fbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3x_0 = 0 - 6 = -6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96812212f50081c6630bc7cc8ae5a7c121d8098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = \\boxed{-6}{-3} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With the old line, we can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> to find its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercept:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b856a3e98d9bfbc086130276cc8ab8a779a415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = 3x_0 + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6d6c98a68157dcd63f7cad6c8b7c9c2d00d06e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x_0 = 0 - 6 = -6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb5aa66c129a7435ecaf39ac3d491a65aaae50e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = \\frac{-6}{3} = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>When a line or point is reflected in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is negated (e.g. reflecting the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1c720139325a2c3491ba41476d225311fcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis would result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad54ab653d3aa7be3416107a9e3ea47007d12f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />).<br />This means that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercept would also be negated, so the new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercept is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cffe28ec339938cc5e476932df774682284ec55a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(-2) = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"134\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fermat\">2024 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" c